      "value": "@{5e59bc346312bf2d549f33ab|full_name} \n\nQuest 3: Qualcomm Snapdragon XR2 Gen 2 (TSMC N4X / 4nm)\n\nSteam frame: Qualcomm Snapdragon 8 Gen 3\n\nBoth devices are using arm64 paired with whatever Qualcomm does for graphics. So the hardware for these two devices are more familiar and compatible with each other than other graphics hardware.\n\nAndroid is based on Linux, like there is a Linux kernel on both. \n\nI think that when valve releases the frame they're going to need to be more specific in what they mean about the frame being a PC. Kind of like how they're no longer talking about 4k as much with the steam machine...\n\nI think there is enough room to do silly things on the steam frame version of VRChat, they might play with loading PC avatars, but the PC shader conversion might not really work, so they'd end up using fallback shaders. Or maybe they'll turn on realtime lighting so avatars can cast shadows\n\nLong story short, the steam frame is mostly being marketed as a wireless streaming PCVR headset, but 16gb of RAM will go a long way l",
