  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-07-27T20:31:19.940Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If the VRChat dev team won't support Linux natively(iOS/android is a waste of resources but you do you) AT LEAST test things with Valve's Proton every major update.\n\nLike it or not, Steam Frame will be running Linux( https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_Frame ), and it will be equally as popular as the Quest 2/3/Pro, as valve seems to be dropping the Index in favor of it, and making it a standalone to compete with Quest.\n\nVRchat will NEED to work properly with Linux. There is no way around it. \n\nValve is pushing Linux with their VR headsets and making them compete with cheaper/standalone options, so the VR market will, quite literally, become 50% Linux overnight.",
